  Q1  IS 13 Hz A FLOOR?   lowest within-target sd 4.8 Hz at gain 0.01600,
      against 12.5 at the derived gain 0.00100
      -> NOT A FLOOR. Every earlier arm ran at ONE gain, so the two-level
         statistic was a property of the protocol, not of the larynx.

  Q2  IS THE AIM INFORMATION-SPECIFIC?  at the best gain 0.01600
      closed |error| 6.0, scrambled 195.5, difference +189.5 +/- 0.3  (623.3 SE)
      gain chosen by the CLOSED arm's own error over 6 rungs, so the
      scrambled contrast at it is not selected on its own value

  THE FEEDBACK LINE RE-OPENS, AND THE REASON IT CLOSED WAS THE GAIN.
  A PERFECT controller holds F1 to 6.0 Hz of an arbitrary target and
  the scrambled control cannot, so this is aim and not drive. aimhold
  measured ONE gain, derived by matching the correction to the error --
  which sets loop gain near 1, where residual error is ~1/2. A
  proportional controller needs L >> 1. The learned-controller question
  is live again, and its upper bound is 6.0 Hz rather than 66.
